## Architecture
- Feature-Sliced layers under src: `shared` (ui kit, i18n, demo store) → `entities` (demo data) → `features` → `widgets` (shells, lists) → `views` (FSD "pages" layer; named views because src/pages is reserved). Routes in src/routes are thin wrappers that import one view. Why: brief requires FSD and no cross-page imports.
- All UI strings live in src/shared/i18n/{tr,en,de}.ts (tr is the typed source); never hardcode copy in components. Why: TR default + EN/DE support.
- No style props; dynamic visuals via Tailwind class maps and tokens in src/styles.css. Why: brief forbids inline styles.
- Prototype only: no backend, no real auth/upload/pairing; demo state in sessionStorage via DemoProvider. Why: brief §8.
- Share schedule controls through features and transfer overviews through widgets across mobile/desktop, with routes remaining thin. Why: avoid divergent controls while keeping desktop layouts distinct.
- Native lock-screen concepts live in a standalone view with local demo states, never browser notifications or native integration. Why: present both platform designs without implying OS functionality in the web prototype.
